  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4611",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to have a target relationship with Serine/threonine-protein kinase NIM1 through multiple independent pathways. The first pathway links Oblonganoside C to Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and then to NIM1. The second pathway connects Oblonganoside C to Caov-4, which is targeted by K-252a, also leading to NIM1. The third pathway shows Oblonganoside C targeting NCI-H1734, which is targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, again leading to NIM1. These findings suggest a consistent pathway where Oblonganoside C modulates the activity of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn affects NIM1. The shared involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol in multiple pathways indicates a potential central role in the mechanism, while the direct interaction of Oblonganoside C with NIM1 is inferred through the intermediate targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Oblonganoside C and NIM1, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
